course: dictionary
lesson: 1368
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Look at the words around the word first. «Hannah showed Mia the toilets, the canteen and where not to sit» tells you the canteen is a place in school.
explain: Here is another clue: «Before the hike, Sam filled his canteen at the tap.» Hikers carry a canteen, which is a small bottle for water. The same word can name a place, a container or a box, so ask: what would fit here?
explain: Try each meaning in the sentence. In «She laid out the canteen of cutlery on the table», a canteen is a box holding knives, forks and spoons. If your meaning still makes sense, you have found it. If not, try the next one.
fact: A canteen is a room or place in a school, factory or office where people buy or get meals.
fact: A canteen is also a small bottle for carrying water, used by soldiers, campers and hikers.
fact: A canteen of cutlery is a box with a set of knives, forks and spoons.
fact: In the US, a canteen in a school is often called a «cafeteria», and in Australia the «tuckshop» is a kind of canteen.
fact: «Many sports canteens sell mostly chocolate and fizzy drinks, so for a long tournament it is wise to pack sandwiches, fruit and water.»
exercise: «Hannah showed Mia the toilets, the canteen and where not to sit.» What is the canteen here? | A box of knives, forks and spoons | A tent for sleeping in | *A room or place where you get meals | A small bottle for carrying water
exercise: Before the hike, Sam filled his canteen at the tap. What is his canteen? | A room where hikers eat | A box of knives, forks and spoons | A tent for sleeping in | *A small bottle for carrying water
exercise: «She laid out the canteen of cutlery on the table.» What is a canteen of cutlery? | *A box with a set of knives, forks and spoons | A table for eating on | A place where meals are cooked | A water bottle for soldiers
test: «Many sports canteens sell mostly chocolate and fizzy drinks.» In this sentence, what is a canteen? | A tent for campers | A box of cutlery | *A place where people buy food and drink | A small bottle for water
test: Ella says a canteen is always a bottle. What is the best reply? | *A canteen can be a place, a bottle or a box, so check the context | A canteen is always a room with food | Ella is right, a canteen is always a bottle | A canteen is a kind of lamp
exam: In «The soldiers filled their canteens at the river», what does canteen mean? | A box of cutlery | A school dining hall | A room for eating | *A small bottle for carrying water
